== The first Linux build of this project (D86's machine), every difference from the Mac ==
   machine   Vultr, 16 vCPU x86_64, 31 GiB, Ubuntu 24.04.5 LTS, kernel 6.8.0-139, glibc 2.39
   Mac       arm64 macOS, Apple clang 21.0.0, Python 3.14.6, torch 2.13.0
   Linux     Ubuntu clang 18.1.3, clang-tidy 18.1.3, opam 2.1.5, cmake 3.28.3,
             Python 3.12.3, torch 2.13.0+cpu, numpy 2.5.2, pandas 3.0.5, pyarrow 25.0.1
   No timing figure is recorded here (stop 35).

-- Builds
L1  oxcaml_setup.sh checked for a command named `bubblewrap`; the Linux package installs
    `bwrap`, so the Linux branch could never pass. FIXED: command:package pairs.
L2  The machine never talks to GitHub (D86, the owner's correction), and the ox opam
    repository and the OxCaml compiler tarball both live there. Shipped from the Mac over
    SSH: the repository checkout (commit f1bd228d), and opam's download cache, which holds
    the compiler tarball under its own sha256 (b7f2248d...). oxcaml_setup.sh takes OX_REPO
    from the environment. GitHub is blocked in the machine's /etc/hosts, so an attempt fails
    rather than succeeds quietly. The switch built from these alone.
L3  rsync kept the Mac's uid 501 on the shipped checkout; git then refused to fetch from a
    repository owned by another user ("dubious ownership"). FIXED: chown to root.
L4  As root, `chmod -R a-w` protects nothing. runs/_weights was made immutable with
    `chattr +i`; a later chown was refused, and so was the write in L10.
L5  shape c8-p10: every gate passed, and the build is silent (0 warnings under -Wall -Wextra
    -Wconversion -Wdouble-promotion -Wshadow -Wold-style-cast -pedantic -Werror).
    cycle_complete.o is 5,470,400 bytes (Mac 1,262,812).
L6  EX1 at 8/10 on Linux: HOLD, 0 of 66,960 outside, margin 1.144x (Mac 1.135x). Not
    bit-identical to the Mac: shard 0 of 1021's worst |err| is 1.129311253e-07 at index
    39819 (Mac 9.734420514e-08 at 20420). Both are inside 51's criterion.
L7  Re-running oxcaml_shape.sh (for EX1) rebuilds the shape directory and removes the
    loopsim and ground_tools built into it; six D85 arms then failed to start. Build
    loopsim AFTER the last shape run. loopsim's build is silent under the same flags.
L8  F' (fprime_setup.sh, SentinelRef, SentinelRetrain) was NOT built on Linux: it serves
    only E1, which the owner deferred. The Darwin-hardcoded paths in d85_e1.sh and
    fprime_ref_retrainer.sh and `pgrep -fl` (which prints only the process name on Linux)
    are therefore not yet exercised; they are owed with E1.

-- Python and the scoring path
L9  lstm.train sets torch to lstm.THREADS = 4 at every call (chosen for the Mac's mixed
    cores). With 16 worker processes that is 64 threads on 16 cores. d86_arms.py sets one
    thread per worker.
L10 (!) Not Linux-specific, found here. 8a35810 (2026-09-21) appended init_weights to the
    weight-cache key; every file in runs/_weights predates it, so today's detectors.fit
    misses all 1,313 and refits. On this machine the immutable store refused the write.
    d86_arms.py reads the fits under their original eight-element key (docs/MODELS.md 79.2).
L11 (!) Not Linux-specific. telemanom.ewma returns NaN at span 1 (its closed form divides by
    (1 - alpha)^k = 0). Span 1 is the identity; d86_arms.py returns the error unchanged.
L12 `pkill -f <pattern>` run over ssh matched the ssh shell's own command line and killed
    it (the pod procedure's warning, met again). Use a pattern anchored at the start.

-- Data
L13 The machine fetched SMAP/MSL and ESA-ADB m1-g8.9.10 directly from R2 with the owner's
    keys in a chmod-600 .env: 3 + 177 Class B, no Class A, every object checked against its
    manifest sha256, reconciled into the ledger from the Mac (+1 A, +181 B with the Mac's
    own read; month 2026-09 then A 240, B 5,921).
L14 The 1,333 files copied from the Mac (runs/_weights, D85's flying model and controls,
    ladder.json, the two SMAP reference artifacts) verified by sha256 on arrival.

-- The scoring path across platforms
L15 (!) D86.A0's matched SMAP/MSL cut is platform-dependent: 5.418254 on x86 Linux against
    D65's 5.288128 on arm64 (stop 62; docs/MODELS.md 79.11). The weights are the same fits
    (S-1's e_s agrees to 6e-8), but on a channel that never moves zstat divides float noise
    by a zero or cancelled trailing sd: A-1's z_res peaks at 30,432 on x86 and 18,445 on
    arm64. A statistic whose tail is set by float noise cannot be reproduced across
    platforms. SMAP/MSL is scored on arm64; the flown C++ core's TrailingWindow uses the same
    1e-12 floor, which is a D87 question.
